      "description": "Location: NYC preferred; remote-friendly (part-time, not fully on-site)\n\nType: Part-time Contract (Contract-to-Hire)\n\nDuration: Month-to-month, or 3 months with possible extension\n\nPay: $30–40/hour, negotiable based on experience\n\nWe welcome candidates from data analytics, data engineering, or traditional software engineering backgrounds who are looking to move into applied AI and LLM work — no prior AI-specific job title required.\n\nAbout Novellia\n\nNovellia is the first and only company that lets anyone in the US gain access to decades of their health data in under 30 seconds, completely free. We help individuals unify their medical records across providers into one continuously updated longitudinal health profile.\n\nWe are building the leading patient-powered real-world data platform for life sciences. Unlike traditional healthcare data providers that rely on fragmented institutional datasets, Novellia enables patients to securely access and authorize 15+ years of longitudinal health records, transforming these complete health journeys into fit-for-purpose datasets for evidence generation, regulatory submissions, and market access.\n\nOur data have been featured in collaborations with leading scientific organizations including ASCO and SABCS/AACR, and we work with top biopharma partners to accelerate research and innovation. Novellia is growing rapidly and backed by tier-1 investors including Spark Capital, Khosla Ventures, Bling Capital, and others.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Data & AI Contractor passionate about LLMs, NLP, and applied AI to join our team and help build AI-powered products and longitudinal healthcare data solutions.\n\nYou'll work closely with the Client Solutions, Data, Engineering, and Product teams to help design and develop best-in-class AI-driven data products while leveraging cutting-edge AI tools to improve productivity, automation, insight generation, and workflows across the company.\n\nThis is a hands-on, part-time contract role where you'll contribute directly to real projects and collaborate across technical and business teams to turn complex healthcare and data challenges into scalable solutions. This is a contract-to-hire track — we're looking for someone we can bring on full-time if it's a strong mutual fit.\n\nWho This Role Is For\n\nThis role is designed for people with roughly 1–3 years of experience in another technical discipline — data analytics, data engineering, software engineering, or similar — who are looking to pivot into AI/LLM work. You don't need a traditional AI/ML resume; you need strong technical fundamentals, curiosity about applied AI, and the drive to build that experience on real projects.\n\nThis Is Where You Come In\n\nWe're a fast-moving startup working on difficult and meaningful problems in healthcare and AI. We value people who are curious, proactive, adaptable, and excited to build.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving ambiguous problems, learning quickly, and working across multiple functions in a highly collaborative environment. You should be comfortable operating with a high level of ownership, moving quickly, and communicating effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\nIf you're excited about AI, healthcare data, and building products that have real-world impact, you'll find the work both challenging and rewarding.\n\nHow You'll Spend Your Time At Novellia\n\nAI Products & Data Solutions\n\nBuild and experiment with NLP- and LLM-based applicationsDevelop solutions involving semantic search, embeddings, summarization, RAG pipelines, AI agents, and prompt engineeringWork on AI-powered products and longitudinal healthcare data solutionsAnalyze structured and unstructured datasets to generate insights and improve product performanceLeverage cutting-edge AI tools to improve workflows, research, automation, and productivityCollaborate closely with Client Solutions, Engineering, Product, and Commercial teams to prototype and iterate quickly\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration & Communication\n\nTranslate business and research questions into scalable technical solutionsPresent findings and explain complex technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholdersSupport internal teams in evaluating new AI workflows, tools, and opportunitiesContribute to building efficient and repeatable processes across projects\n\nRequirements\n\nExperience & Expertise\n\n~1–3 years of professional experience in data analytics, data engineering, software engineering, or a related technical roleStrong coding skills in SQL and Python (particularly with common ML/data libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, PyTorch, or TensorFlow)Solid foundation in, or strong self-driven exposure to, machine learning, modeling, statistics, and data analysisStrong communication skills and the ability to explain complex solutions to technical and non-technical audiencesComfortable working in a fast-paced startup environment with ambiguity and rapid iterationStrong organizational skills and attention to detailExperience working collaboratively across teams is a plus\n\nCore Technical Areas\n\nHands-on experience with LLMs and applied AISolid grounding in NLP (natural language processing)Experience with semantic search / embeddingsExperience with summarization techniquesExperience with RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) pipelines\n\nBonus Points\n\nExperience with Hugging Face, LangChain, LlamaIndex, vector databases, or cloud platforms (GCP/AWS/Azure)Personal AI projects, hackathons, research, or open-source contributionsExperience building AI copilots, chatbots, or agent-based workflows\n\nWhy Join Novellia?\n\nWork directly on real AI products and healthcare data challengesGain hands-on experience with cutting-edge AI technologies and workflowsCollaborate with a highly ambitious and technical teamFlexible, part-time engagement built around a career pivot into AIContract-to-hire track, with the opportunity to convert to a full-time role for the right fit\n\nAdditional Information\n\nDon't meet every requirement? Studies show women and people of color are less likely to apply unless they meet 100% of qualifications. At Novellia, we're committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. If you're excited about this role, we encourage you to apply even if your experience doesn't perfectly match every qualification.\n\nU.S. Applicants Only",
